# Terraform
.terraform/
crash.log
*.tfplan

# Provider lock files ARE committed. A module pinned by tag with providers left
# to float is half a pin, and the floating half is the dangerous one: the
# bpg/proxmox constraint here is ~> 0.101, which admits everything below 1.0 on
# a provider whose own comments call the SDN resources "still settling". A fresh
# init could therefore resolve a provider that plans a replacement against live
# SDN objects.
#
# The fabric's state is committed here. It is five substrate-owned resources
# with one operator, and a repository is a perfectly good home for that: clone
# gives you code and state together, and history gives you every prior state
# with no restore path to rehearse.
#
# Tenants do NOT keep state here - they are not here at all (ADR-0006), and
# their state lives in the substrate's store or wherever they choose to carry it
# (ADR-0007).
#
# Either way the invariant holds: whatever holds state is a secret store the
# moment state contains a secret, so no resource is declared whose value cannot
# be re-derived. Backups and any *.tfvars that might carry a token stay out.
*.tfstate.backup
*.auto.tfvars
secrets.auto.tfvars

# Rendered credentials, if anyone copies one in here
*.env

# Terraform lock files from an interrupted run
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
